WEBVTT

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.030
We're here!

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.780
Hurry up, Kousei!

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.160
O-Okay!

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.540
Could you park the car for us, Takahiko?

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.710
Sure. I'll catch up with everyone later.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.050
Shall we go, Tsubaki?

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:26.970
Okay.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:31.680
Hiroko, it's been a while since we came here just to watch.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.720
You're right.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.140
I'll enjoy today with that in mind.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:38.350
Wow, cute!

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.560
You look really good in your dress!

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.150
Thanks!

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.900
Hey, let's have our picture taken!

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.570
Setsu's dad!

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:50.610
Can you take a picture of me and Setsu?

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.490
Of course I can.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:54.530
All right. Can you two stand next to each other here?

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:55.660
I'm taking it.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.410
Now, say cheese!

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.440
You're always eating soda-flavored popsicles.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.310
Do you like it, Emi?

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:48.150
Yeah.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:52.610
It looks like Mako's seventh. I can't wait to see her play!

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.490
She looked really nervous, so I wonder if she'll be okay.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:04.250
<i>I should've joined Yuuichi and his friends to play dodgeball instead.</i>

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.420
Watari, hurry up! It's this way!

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.790
Hey, wait!

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.250
There was a pretty la—

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.500
Shut up!

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.010
No. 5, Mr. Arima Kousei.

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:22.890
Huh?

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.740
What's up with him?

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.450
He's a bundle of nerves.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.030
I did it!

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.710
What's gotten into you, Emi?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.130
You ran out of there without listening to Mako's performance!

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.180
No. 5, Mr. Arima Kousei.

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:27.470
Arima... Kousei...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.640
Emi!

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.060
What are you doing?! You could get hurt!

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:35.020
You could've at least picked the slides instead!

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.610
I'm gonna be a pianist!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.330
I thought you played the violin, Kao.

00:05:47.330 --> 00:05:49.200
I used to play piano when I was really little.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.750
Let's watch them play for a bit, and then we can go shopping.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.130
Just for a bit, okay?

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.420
Thanks.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.670
Arima Kousei is definitely going to win again.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.470
The kids in this neighborhood don't stand a chance with him around.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.180
Are you worried?

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.850
I'm not!

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:16.150
<i>Because Arima Kousei isn't being himself right now.</i>

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.360
<i>Arima?</i>

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.940
<i>Alone? There's nobody with him?</i>

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:23.650
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.950
<i>I'll make a jab at him.</i>

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:36.130
Oh, I feel like having a popsicle!

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:43.220
Hey, this is one of those you can split in half!

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.380
I don't know if I can eat both halves myself.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.100
What should I do?

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.180
<i>Completely ignored!</i>

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.640
Long time no see, Ms. Ochiai.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:57.560
Indeed it has been, Mr. Takayanagi.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.070
There's actually a kid I've been working with lately.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.820
There is?

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.740
<i>A grade schooler.</i>

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.950
<i>With this snobbish control freak?</i>

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:11.160
His name is Aiza Takeshi.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.540
This boy is going to be the next star.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.830
Nice to meet you.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.170
It was a pleasure seeing you again.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.960
Teaching piano...

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:25.220
or should I say disciplining children, appears to be your forte, Ms. Ochiai.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.220
Children aren't as easy to handle as you might think.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:32.600
Coming off too strong and putting on airs can test patience.

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.140
Of the child.

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:38.650
Your advice is rather hard to swallow.

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.570
Oh, I was simply giving you some forewarning.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.660
<i>I get a transformation belt just for entering.</i>

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.450
<i>If I win, I get a die-cast robot.</i>

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:57.960
<i>Piano's a breeze!</i>

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.710
Wait!

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:08.430
Wait for me, Brother!

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.760
I said wait!

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.020
<i>Amazing!</i>

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.350
<i>That was just amazing!</i>

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:18.890
<i>He memorized the entire score through and through!</i>

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.570
<i>Everyone's freaking out, but he doesn't even bat an eyelash!</i>

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:26.690
<i>Just like a gunman from a Western film!</i>

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:34.080
<i>A heart of steel.</i>

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.790
<i>Unrivaled skills.</i>

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:38.370
<i>He leaves the stage while keeping that composure.</i>

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.420
<i>He's like a die-cast robot!</i>

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.880
<i>He's full of power and really cool.</i>

00:08:46.340 --> 00:08:48.880
<i>Arima's a superhero!</i>

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:03.020
Darn it! I'm off tempo again!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.520
Why can't I play like him?

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.940
<i>Just what kind of practicing does he even do?</i>

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.610
<i>Did they turn him into a robot or something?</i>

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:14.950
<i>All Mr. Takayanagi makes me do is
play the same music over and over.</i>

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.420
I'll just have to uncover the secrets to his playing myself!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.220
Huh? That's weird.

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:33.010
I could've sworn it was around here.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.060
Um, excuse me.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:36.720
Huh?

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.720
Do you know where Hibari Elementary is?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:44.270
Oh, if you want to get there,
keep going straight and turn left at the second alley.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.110
Thank you very much!

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:50.820
There are lots of alleys here, so it can be confusing.

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:54.200
A cake shop?

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:56.450
Yeah. We're opening at the beginning of next month.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.120
Ma... Ma...

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.700
Ma Fille.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:04.580
It means "my daughter" in French.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.250
I see.

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:08.550
Well, thank you very much!

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:09.510
Sure!

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:11.590
Make sure you come by once we've opened!

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:12.930
I will!

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:24.060
<i>There's an event going on at my school, so I've got the day off.</i>

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:26.360
<i>Chances like this don't come easily!</i>

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:29.230
<i>There he is!</i>

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:35.990
Hey, turn around

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.830
Hey, listen to me

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.870
I'm not that small

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.330
My voice is clear

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:48.130
I'm not making myself taller than I am

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:52.590
Look, I can do it

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:56.010
Look at me

00:10:56.390 --> 00:11:04.940
I can shine in the sunlight

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:01.770
Okay! Time to hear you practice!

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:14.570
I know that I will be fine

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.450
<i>Whoa.</i>

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:16.160
<i>He's been at it for an hour.</i>

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:21.370
Even when doubt haunts me

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:20.370
<i>How can he play for so long without tripping up or missing a single note?</i>

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.830
<i>His focus is outta this world.</i>

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:31.880
I only want to see you smile

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:35.510
I don't care about all the others

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:44.270
For that I can weather the storm

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.390
<i>You're kidding me.</i>

00:11:38.390 --> 00:11:42.010
<i>All he's been doing is practicing the same music repeatedly.</i>

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.560
<i>And the sun's already setting!</i>

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:51.860
Desperately I clung to the one I admired

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:58.860
And acted like nothing was wrong

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:02.450
<i>All he did was those tiresome and boring repetitions.</i>

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:07.330
It hurts a little to remember it

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.000
<i>He probably plays the piece until it becomes a part of him,</i>

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.040
<i>until he can replicate the piece down to every note and accent.</i>

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:11.540
<i>Over and over...</i>

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.830
<i>He's first again! That's amazing!</i>

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:48.370
<i>Darn it... It wasn't enough!</i>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.500
<i>It wasn't anywhere </i>close<i> to enough!</i>

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:01.760
<i>I practice at least five hours every day.
I even woke up early, which I hate doing.</i>

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.510
<i>Until I could replicate the piece and call it my own.</i>

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:06.720
<i>It'll be okay!</i>

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.600
<i>I'm a die-cast robot too!</i>

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:13.480
The beginning should be played with confidence, hinting sorrow and anxiousness.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:16.650
Let it cry out and ring here.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.240
Like the setting sun in the spring that releases warm colors into the sky.

00:13:20.530 --> 00:13:21.740
<i>What's this?</i>

00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:25.240
No. 5, Ms. Igawa! Please get ready.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.830
Huh? What do you want?

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:27.450
Oh, uh...

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:28.620
Do you have a problem?

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.910
No, just...

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:48.100
<i>What was with her performance?</i>

00:13:48.100 --> 00:13:50.640
<i>It didn't follow the manuscript at all!</i>

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.400
<i>Yet... Yet, why?</i>

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.820
Take that, fake Arima.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:20.710
You made the top ten.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:21.920
Good job.

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:26.640
Arima's a competition maniac who's played on stage countless times.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.140
Someday, you also will—

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:29.140
You're wrong!

00:14:29.140 --> 00:14:30.180
Takeshi?

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.730
<i>You're wrong...</i>

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:32.810
<i>It was her!</i>

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:35.480
She showed me up!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.190
<i>Igawa Emi!</i>

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.990
Hey, Takeshi!

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.580
We need one more person!

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.250
Can you fill in?

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:55.460
Yeah!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:02.340
Sorry, I think I'm gonna go practice piano instead.

00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:03.340
Okay.

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:04.880
See ya later, then.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.350
Darn it!

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.150
<i>I love soccer, but I haven't played it at all.</i>

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.400
<i>I wake up early every day and practice five hours straight.</i>

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.530
<i>I don't even take holidays off.</i>

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.910
<i>New toys? I don't need them.</i>

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:31.410
<i>And I'll turn down my friends when they invite me outside.</i>

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:35.330
<i>I want to become the perfect superhero too!</i>

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:41.420
<i>I want to hear Arima giving it his all too!</i>

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:47.130
<i>I know that I don't have an unwavering heart—
that there's a lot I need to work on.</i>

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:51.050
<i>That guy does way more than I do.</i>

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:55.930
<i>He's probably steeled his heart and is sitting at the piano by himself!</i>

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:58.560
Go, Kousei!

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:01.320
Go, Kousei! Jump!

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:04.570
Arima?!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.860
Give it all you got this time!

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:09.700
You were the one who said you'd go again!

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.450
If you're a man, you'll go for it!

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.330
He did it!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:19.250
That's what I'm talking about! What a man!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.250
It's my turn next!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.750
This is fun!

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.550
Me too, then!

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:33.060
<i>So that's how he looks like when he's laughing.</i>

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:43.110
I've made up my mind!

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:46.900
I'm gonna play soccer tomorrow!

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:56.830
As usual, Arima won again.

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.210
He played the piece perfectly through and through.

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:01.120
It was completely flawless.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.750
Don't you feel bitter?

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:05.550
'Course I do!

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:10.760
But I'll make sure to squash him at the second round when there's more people watching!

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:13.140
And how do you feel?

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.010
I couldn't care less. It's all in the past.

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:16.930
Huh?

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:22.940
I try to pick pieces that Arima might play, but it looks like I chose the wrong one.

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:24.770
That's why I couldn't care less.

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.650
It wasn't the same piece as Arima's.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:31.740
Oh, I see. You wanna face Arima
head-on by playing the same piece!

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.280
You've got guts!

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:34.910
Just like a guy!

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.620
I'm a girl!

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:38.620
Hot!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.420
It's not about winning or losing.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.710
All I want...

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.050
is for him to return.

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:57.220
Ow!

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:04.520
How about a short break?

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:07.480
You've been overworking yourself lately.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:09.940
I'm okay.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.320
I remember what you told me before.

00:18:14.070 --> 00:18:18.990
The harder I wish, the more my music will reply in turn.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:21.540
The piano will resound with it.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.540
Did I say that?

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.080
I was right!

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:30.130
Beethoven's 3rd movement, <i>Appassionata</i>!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:34.840
<i>That's why I want my playing to resound.</i>

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:44.020
<i>Like always, he plays by the manuscript.</i>

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.730
<i>A completely flawless Arima Kousei.</i>

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:48.650
<i>But today, I'll beat him.</i>

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:51.650
<i>I'll make him remember with these hands.</i>

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:55.070
<i>The real him.</i>

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:01.620
Good job.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.290
You did pretty well today too.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:05.170
Thanks.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:09.290
Is your baby ready to come out yet, Hiro?

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.880
Hm... I don't think it'll be long.

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.010
Oh, I felt my baby kick!

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:16.390
Your baby is kicking your stomach?

00:19:16.390 --> 00:19:17.680
That's right.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:20.010
I wonder if it's a boy.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.260
You might be right.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:24.770
Please have a doctor examine her tomorrow.

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:25.810
Of course.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:27.810
We're very sorry, Ms. Ochiai.

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.360
I should apologize as well.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.530
I didn't notice until now.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:34.400
Why you didn't tell anyone until it started to really hurt?

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.180
Is something getting built over there?

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.890
Kaori!

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:01.260
Oh! Coming!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:06.690
Yo!

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.770
I heard you got tendinitis.

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:13.570
Are you better now?

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:16.820
I'll have you know, you'll never see me withdraw.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.660
Huh? That wasn't what I asked!

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:23.330
Anyway, you're in sixth grade now
and you're <i>still</i> eating that popsicle?

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:26.790
And I'm pretty sure you were eating <i>that</i> the day we first met, Takeshi.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:29.290
Was I really?

00:20:32.170 --> 00:20:33.460
Hey, Emi.

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:39.340
When we become junior high or even high schoolers,

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.260
do you think we'll be playing the piano still?

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.310
Who knows.

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:48.140
There's one thing I figured out when I took a break because of my injury, though.

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:54.650
I've come to love playing the piano.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.700
I wonder if Arima feels the same way.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:04.280
What?! How am I supposed to know?!

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.290
Why are you getting so mad?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.000
